      "headings": [
        "The Seaweed Canyon Cardiovascular Physiology Laboratory",
        "Seaweed Cardiovascular Physiology Core Services",
        "Directors"
      ],
      "text": "The Seaweed Canyon Cardiovascular Physiology Laboratory Seaweed Cardiovascular Physiology Core Services (Not limited to the following) Invasive left heart and right heart functions and pathological cardiac models studies: Hemodynamics with or without pressure volume loops studies with various agents' injections. Blood pressure measurement in conscience mice with telemetry, in anesthetized mice with catheters. Electrocardiogram (ECG) in conscience mice using telemetry, or under anesthetized with isoflurane Intra-cardiac pacing with electric programming stimulation Transverse aortic constriction (TAC) and post TAC pressure gradient measurements Myocardial infarction Ischemia reperfusion Mini pump implantation Neonatal mice apex resection Aortic stenosis wire injury Intra- cardiac, ventricles and venous injections of virus, cells or experiment agents. Blood and tissue collections 2. Non-invasive cardiac function studies: Echocardiography: Pulsed-Wave Doppler (aortic flow and pulmonary flow) 2D (chamber size and function, aortic arch size) 4 Chamber view with Pulsed-Wave Doppler and Tissue Doppler Strain Analysis Other measurements Tail cuff Treadmill Directors Dr. Eric D. Adler and Dr. Ju Chen, Co-Directors, 2020-present Dr. Kirk L. Peterson, Associate Director, 1988 – 2005, and Director, 2005-2020 Dr. John Ross, Jr., Director, 1972 - 2005 Dr. Eugene Braunwald, Director, 1968 - 1972 Dr. Dean Franklin, Founding Director, 1965-1970",
